<title>JAPAN: Wakayama Petroleum to shut topper from mid-May.</title>
<headline>Wakayama Petroleum to shut topper from mid-May.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wakayama Petroleum Refining Co Ltd said on Friday it would close its 50,000 barrel-per-day crude distillation unit at its Kainan plant in central Japan for about one month from mid-May for routine maintenance.</p>
<p>The refiner is owned 50 percent by Mitsubishi Oil Co Ltd, and the rest by several other companies.</p>
